      "id": "n1eqsow",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.1 Monitor"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Monitors display visual information as soft copy output, categorized into CRT, LCD, LED, and OLED technologies.",
        "Printers generate permanent physical output (hard copy) and are divided into Impact and Non-Impact printers.",
        "Plotters are specialized output devices designed for vector graphics, blueprint printing, and high-precision CAD drawings.",
        "Speakers convert electronic digital audio signals into audible acoustic sound waves.",
        "Non-impact printers like Laser and Inkjet provide higher speed, superior resolution, and quieter operation compared to impact printers."
      ],
      "id": "knpaybn"
    },
