    {
      "id": "n8pcf7j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.4 Speaker"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Impact printers (e.g., Dot Matrix) use physical striking mechanisms, while Non-Impact printers (Laser, Inkjet) use non-contact technology.",
        "DPI (Dots Per Inch) determines printer output quality, while PPM (Pages Per Minute) measures printer speed.",
        "Laser printers use electrostatic toner powder and a drum mechanism, making them the fastest non-impact printers for text."
      ],
      "id": "18qujet"
    },
